## Codebase Diagnosis (What I Found)

### Current Architecture
```
Input SMILES
    → atom/bond embeddings (300-dim)
    → 5x GINEConv layers (300-dim)
    → GlobalAttention Pooling
    → Linear(300→512)
    → 2-layer MLP head → output
```

### Critical Weaknesses Found

| Issue | Location | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| **XGBoost baseline** (not GNN) used for per-endpoint training | `model-training/scripts/train_models.py` | Your "GNN" paper uses XGBoost in production |
| **Training from scratch** — no pretrained molecular encoder | `train_attention_gin.py` L.279 | Costs 3-5% AUC vs. pretrained models |
| **Single global pos_weight=3.0** for all 12 tasks | `train_attention_gin.py` L.479 | Wrong for tasks with 30:1+ imbalance (NR-AR has <5% positive rate) |
| **CosineAnnealingLR** with fixed T_max=epochs | `train_attention_gin.py` L.348 | Decays too aggressively for fine-tuning |
| **No scaffold split** during training | `train_attention_gin.py` L.99 | Inflated random-split AUC — not reproducible |
| **Morgan fingerprint only** (no MACCS, no RDKit descriptors combined with GNN) | `train_models.py` L.44 | Missing ~2% AUC from descriptor fusion |
| **Single-task heads** per endpoint | `attention_ginet.py` | Multi-task sharing boosts rare endpoints (NR-AR-LBD, NR-PPAR-gamma) |
| **No test-time uncertainty** | All models | Reviewers now expect calibration (ECE) |
| **ClinTox: only 1,478 samples, 25:1 imbalance** | dataset | Nothing fixes this except frozen encoder + focal loss |
| **CUDA not available on dev machine** | Hardware | All training must be pushed to Colab/Kaggle GPU |

