## Practical Notes for Your Hardware Setup

Since **CUDA is not available** on your local machine, here's the recommended workflow:

### Kaggle (Recommended — Free T4 GPU)
- 30 hours/week GPU quota
- Persistent dataset storage (up to 100 GB)
- Use it for: pre-training (Week 6-7), fine-tuning sweeps (Week 8)
- Cost: **Free**

### Google Colab Pro (~$10/month)
- A100 or V100 GPU, higher RAM
- Better for long training runs (pre-training)
- Use it for: anything requiring >6 hours
- Cost: **~$10/month**

### Local Machine (CPU only — good for)
- Dataset preprocessing
- TabPFN, SNN, XGBoost baselines
- Debugging training scripts
- Paper writing

